{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1553771-what-fictional-universe-s-would-you-live-in","id":1553771,"title":"What fictional universe's would you live in?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-09-12T11:48:34-07:00","id":1553771,"title":"What fictional universe's would you live in?","content":"Just something fun to partake in.<br /> <br /> Star Wars. Advanced technology, alien species and mystical arts. I would like to be in that universe.<br /> <br /> Shadowrun. Mythical creatures, advanced technology and magic and a great setting and I noticed that I love having creature comforts like electricity, medicine and plumbing.<br /> <br /> Those are what I can think of right now as I have to be off to work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-12T12:54:06-07:00","id":1553772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1553771-what-fictional-universe-s-would-you-live-in#post1553771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Shadowrun. Mythical creatures, advanced technology and magic and a great setting and I noticed that I love having creature comforts like electricity, medicine and plumbing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, as long as you're a well-paid corporate SINner you have it. Everyone else's access to those last three is much more... sporadic. And they have to make their living shoveling the shit of said mythical creatures off the streets for peanuts, or making more through the high-stakes, high risk world of Future Crime.<br /> <br /> Also every few years there's another thing that snatches bodies. Frequently a malign spiritual entity, but sometimes it's tech, like with the nanomachines that rewrote your brain to be like an AI, or cyberjacks allowing your brain to be hacked by something from within the very questionably sourced internet (made by linking together a hundred people with internet mind powers... only they died, so whatever's keeping it up is anyone's guess).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-12T14:26:54-07:00","id":1553775,"title":"","content":"At my age, probably some sort of nice comfortable slice of life anime, to be honest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-12T16:20:33-07:00","id":1553779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1553771-what-fictional-universe-s-would-you-live-in?p=1553775#post1553775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At my age, probably some sort of nice comfortable slice of life anime, to be honest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Second that.<br /> <br /> As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> made clear with Shadowrun's example, the problem with the question is that most &quot;exciting and interesting&quot; places would be quite horrible to live in.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty happy in a world where I can live exciting or gut-wrenching stories through media, I just wish it was safer and sucked less.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-14T19:50:04-07:00","id":1553826,"title":"","content":"<i>Game of Thrones</i>, provided I had some sort of supernatural-edge; it is just me, or would the world of Westeros, be an awesome setting for a WoD, or CoD game? All the stuff from the books (Dance of the Dragons (House of the Dragon) or Game of Thrones, can be going on in the background while your characters deal with supernatural-threats; it would be a great Mage or Werewolf game, for sure. <br /> <br /> Any movie about the future, be it Minority-Report, Logan's Run etc. I would just enjoy being alive in the next century. <br /> <br /> And any book about the past; when I read a book about Queen Elizabeth's London, I have a world, in my head; and certain things I like, like, everyone back then spoke like a pirate. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1553771-what-fictional-universe-s-would-you-live-in#post1553771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just something fun to partake in.<br /> <br /> . . .</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, we're currently living in Cyperpunk: 2020, sans the cyberware. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-14T23:06:11-07:00","id":1553831,"title":"","content":"StarFinder is another favorite of mine. I like the mystery of what caused history and time go off kilter. In the setting only the last 320 years of history can be accurately recalled by the denizens of that universe.<br /> <br /> For people with comparatively short lifespans like humans this isn't a big deal, but for species with much longer lifespans like Elves, Dwarves, Dragons and Gods this is disconerting to say the least.<br /> <br /> Voltron I would to work on the robotic lions and test them out when we update the technology.<br /> <br /> James Bond, I always loved the Q character and all his gadgets that he came up with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-15T10:54:15-07:00","id":1553838,"title":"","content":"As enticing as living in another world is (especially NOW), most of the fiction I consume would be a nightmare to live in;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I read a LOT of Lovecraftian fiction and that\u2019s completely off the table (even if I can remember a few spells to cause Cthugha to blast an area to ash). My stock of Forgotten Realms, Dragonlance, and other such D&amp;D novels prove life there is not easier by any stretch, even with the presence of magic. The Potterverse is right out, as is the world of Dresden Files, I do not need to be the random recipient of magical fallout, and in the Dresdenverse if I had magic it would ruin my electronics. The classic mythic world of earth (things like Odyssey, prose Eddas, etc.) is insane by any metric, and to be lain down and avoided.<br /> <br /> Anyone who has read comics knows that living in the world of comics is insanity. That goes double for mangas. I almost said I\u2019d live in the X-men\u2019s universe, but since I\u2019m already a minority, it would take alpha-level mutant powers AT LEAST to make it worth adding additional oppression to my plate.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-15T11:53:35-07:00","id":1553839,"title":"","content":"I feel the same way about Warhammer 40 K. I wouldn't want to visit that setting and let alone live there. It would have to be a far off world that the Imperium, Alederai, Drukari, Orks, Tyranids, Necrons and Chaos Gods didn't know about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-15T15:17:06-07:00","id":1553842,"title":"","content":"Ah so it\u2019s gameworlds as well? Well then to continue;<br /> <br /> <br /> I\u2019ve already expressed that living in anything D&amp;D (or D&amp;D-adjacent) isn\u2019t any better and might be worse depending on the setting.<br /> <br /> So moving on, the WOD is completely out of the picture as god has literally left the building in that setting. Even if you are a Mage the whole of reality is constantly punching you in the dick, so it\u2019s not worth it.<br /> <br /> Living in the Trinity Continuum means I\u2019d better have powers or it\u2019s not worth it. And if I DO have powers I\u2019m not <i>just</i> going to be taint-battered, I\u2019m gonna be <b>deep fried</b> in it till I ascend. That or my psiad powers will have me standing further and further away from baseline humanity and all of their grotesque stupidity. That goes for the setting of Mutants &amp; masterminds since it\u2019s too close to comic world, and we already know that\u2019s insanity.<br /> <br /> Scion may be fun to play, but it would still be awful to live in that setting. Being quasi-divine doesn\u2019t make this better, it just makes it worse. And the prospect of getting swept up into a fatebond because some jackass can\u2019t keep their \u201cpowers\u201d in their pants makes my butt hurt pre-emptively.<br /> <br /> I remember a day in my far-off youth where I was a big Star Wars fan, but now if you told me I could live in that universe I\u2019d tell you to quit smoking rocks. Not merely because of all the licensing idiocy lately, mostly because I can\u2019t recall a single world in that setting that was worth living on. They\u2019re all wasteland outposts or wretched hives of scum and villainy, and I get enough of that in the American midwest.<br /> <br /> <br /> If we move into video gameworlds it gets worse!<br /> <br /> <br /> All of the Final Fantasy multiverse (since it\u2019s established that all those worlds are separate dimensions) may have a semi-consistent set of jobs and skills, but they are also prone to being infested with evil empires, irate godlings, and cosmic horrors disguised as \u201csecret bosses\u201d. I don\u2019t need to have to level up to level 12, or go impotent from a Mako infusion JUST to pick up my amazon deliveries.<br /> <br /> The world of the Mana series seems to have a very unusual tidal magic axiom that I find...distasteful. Which is too bad since ti seems pretty peaceful there.<br /> <br /> The world of Suikoden is extremely war-prone, so is that of the Shining franchise, so life will be harder than normal due to constant wartime economy fatigue.<br /> <br /> SMT &amp; Persona games may be charming, but living in those worlds means literally walking into a materialized crack dream and/or psychosis. I don\u2019t have enough psychology background to deal with that every single day.<br /> <br /> The worlds of Xenosaga, Bioshock, and Mass Effect prove that post-scarcity is not only a myth, it\u2019s a pipe-dream. Borderlands is prolly just a few decades away from real life.<br /> <br /> It should go without saying that any world infected with the corporate horseshit of Weyland-Yutani, Umbrella, Mobius, Shin-Ra, or frankly ANY other megacorporation isn\u2019t worth living in.<br /> <br /> Fargaia, the world of Wild Arms exists just to prove that it can, and is even more pre-destroyed than FF7\u2019s world is. Plus, the American Wild West was NOT a good time, no matter what some dumb-ass tries to tell you. Adding magic to that mess would just make a BIGGER mess.<br /> <br /> The setting of Ultima was an isekai dumping ground last I checked, which is all the more reason to leave it alone.<br /> <br /> Phantasy Star has the interesting background of an omnipotent cosmic horror deciding it has nothing better to do than utterly destroy all things vaguely human (parmian) for the sake of completion. All the hyper-space age tech in the universe doesn\u2019t make up for that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-15T18:25:38-07:00","id":1553845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1553771-what-fictional-universe-s-would-you-live-in?p=1553842#post1553842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Phantasy Star has the interesting background of an omnipotent cosmic horror deciding it has nothing better to do than utterly destroy all things vaguely human (parmian) for the sake of completion. All the hyper-space age tech in the universe doesn\u2019t make up for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least in <i>Phantasy Star</i> shit only hits the fan every thousand years, so you have a chance of a peaceful life in the interregnum.<br /> <br /> <i>Game of Thrones</i> seems to be among the few Medieval Fantasy settings where magic didn't solve absolutely any of the problems of medieval life, and a lot of false medieval stereotypes are true there, so you have plague, hunger, shit everywhere, rotten food, and everything and everyone smells bad.<br /> <br /> If we stay true to the most tame media (which does include the videogames), the world of Pokemon would probably be among the least unpleasant for the common folk. Kinda dangerous, but non-lethal, and you don't need to be special to do some cool stuff in your life, but hold a regular, stable job and go back home to play videogames.<br /> <br /> On most other places the very best life I can get isn't fundamentally very different from what I already have. The real world has plenty of interesting things to do if you have the money for it, and that doesn't change in many non-awful settings. A lot of expectations about how life would be in other worlds rely on not being an average person there, and you can go wild if instead you just imagine how life would be in this world if you were not an average person here. It would be nice to be filthy rich anywhere, including right here and now.<br /> <br /> Pokemon is a world where you can have a fantastical companion even if you're an idiot, or homeless, or abused at work. Being aristocracy or special in any other way isn't at all required. On top of that they seem to have a reasonably stable society with at least basic welfare policies and services.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-20T18:55:36-07:00","id":1553945,"title":"","content":"Lovecraft, Warhammer; Mage: Ascension; no thank you; if I had to live in a fictional-setting, I choose Star Trek, with their utopian-society, living-credits economy, advance technology etc. I'd probably live a long-life, on some world without ever stepping foot on a starship, with excellent health-benefits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-09T00:22:08-08:00","id":1557403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1553771-what-fictional-universe-s-would-you-live-in#post1553771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Shadowrun.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You do realize Shadowrun is just Cyberpunk with magic in it, right? Not only that, but getting yourself cybernetically augmented weakens your soul and your capacity to wield magic.<br /> <br /> Shadowrun exists in a setting where most forms of technology require a data jack to interact with. Meaning you need at least a rudimentary level of augmentation just to function in modern society.<br /> <br /> Also, have fun surfing the internet, with the knowledge that there sentient AI prowling the system, who may be trying to fry your brain!<br /> <br /> Finally, you have to confront the knowledge that in Shadowrun, humans are now effectively the worst race in the game, due to how basic they are. Every other race in the setting greatly outperforms humans in some category or another. They're even starting to lose the advantage of superior numbers, because of how quickly Orcs breed, having an average of 3 to 4 children with each pregnancy.<br /> <br /> <br /> --------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> Personally, I'd probably like to live in the world of <b>Pathfinder</b>. I am firmly of the mind that Pathfinder is superior to D&amp;D, ever since I started looking into it, and I love the new material they've been churning out for Second edition.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> might also be appealing, as the lack of metaplot and self contained narratives make the setting far less of a convoluted mess than World of Darkness ended up becoming.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lone Wolf Fists</b> may be a post apocalyptic setting, but it's also one that features super powered, magical kung fu inspired by popular anime from the 60's - 80's period. I'd have to get off my ass and do some exercise, but I'd eventually get strong enough to knock down skyscrapers by punching them!<br /> <br /> <br /> Finally, there's the <b>Kings of Hell </b>universe, which just seems like a ton of fun to live in!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-14T17:27:33-07:00","id":1558860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1553771-what-fictional-universe-s-would-you-live-in?p=1553772#post1553772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, as long as you're a well-paid corporate SINner you have it. Everyone else's access to those last three is much more... sporadic. And they have to make their living shoveling the shit of said mythical creatures off the streets for peanuts, or making more through the high-stakes, high risk world of Future Crime.<br /> <br /> Also every few years there's another thing that snatches bodies. Frequently a malign spiritual entity, but sometimes it's tech, like with the nanomachines that rewrote your brain to be like an AI, or cyberjacks allowing your brain to be hacked by something from within the very questionably sourced internet (made by linking together a hundred people with internet mind powers... only they died, so whatever's keeping it up is anyone's guess).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You forgot the systemic racism, the vastly different life spans (50 years for Orcs, 40 for Trolls), the existence of an entire mega corporation that regularly participates in blood magic...<br /> <br /> Or the fact any of the more supernatural elements of Shadowrun can only exist within the planet's atmosphere, due to the existence of its mana sphere. If you try to leave the planet, your spells will stop working, and your meta gene may become suppressed again.<br /> <br /> Finally, there's the Dragons, who despite the fact nearly all of them are power hungry tyrants, the world still needs them around. In the video games, if you go alongside the plan to release a virus that wipes them all out, the magic of the world surges to unstable levels, and results in a Lovecraftian apocalypse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-16T07:37:52-07:00","id":1558890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1553771-what-fictional-universe-s-would-you-live-in?p=1558860#post1558860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You forgot the systemic racism</div> </div> </div> </div>Double the systemic issues - meta-prejudice and ethnic-based racism!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the vastly different life spans (50 years for Orcs, 40 for Trolls) </div> </div> </div>It's been established now that anyone living in the shit conditions of the sprawls that most orks and trolls live in would have truncated lifespans, so it's actually worse, but cuts along a slightly different stratum. Orks and trolls, as of 6e, don't keel over dead at 40 or 50-ish, respectively, just because the calendar year passed by. In fact, satyr metavariant orks have dwarf-length lifespans and both ogres and oni live 10-15% longer than humans if they can get comparable living conditions. That, of course, is the rub, and why it's always a Good Karma worthy act to punch Humanis thugs (with Killing Hands or a cyberarm).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the existence of an entire mega corporation that regularly participates in blood magic... </div> </div> </div>The writing likes to go all in on that until someone remembers that they have at least the appearance of a coherent setting to maintain and walks some of it back. Also, the elements most in favor of the blood magic keep ending up getting killed (Mr. Darke is now under a pile of bodies).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or the fact any of the more supernatural elements of Shadowrun can only exist within the planet's atmosphere, due to the existence of its mana sphere. If you try to leave the planet, your spells will stop working, and your meta gene may become suppressed again. </div> </div> </div>Metagene shutoff is only if you go by Equinox, which has been separated from canon. Earthdawn also now operates in an alternate canon space, hence why their orks do magically drop dead in their 40s. The gahad burns through them.<br /> <br /> (Also, Ares has a satellite in low orbit that has enough cultivated greenery to have its own mini-magic sphere. Its purpose is to maintain a gateway to the Hive, the home plane of the Invae, so that Ares can send over operatives to inhabit bug bodies and scour the massive, universal graveyard of whatever the Hive took in over its existence for alien artifacts.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Finally, there's the Dragons, who despite the fact nearly all of them are power hungry tyrants, the world still needs them around. In the video games, if you go alongside the plan to release a virus that wipes them all out, the magic of the world surges to unstable levels, and results in a Lovecraftian apocalypse. </div> </div> </div>That had a lot to do with how the magic was already spiking over where it should be in the cycle and the Kill All Dragons plague from Dragonfall (it's optional bad ending, anyway) killed off Dunkelzahn early, which means that he didn't get to go through with his ritual suicide to even out the magic level that was excessive due to the Ghost Dance ritual practice (which was just Call Forth the Maelstrom, formula courtesy of Aina's half-horror son Thais). Also, no one managed to work out spell matrices in time to deal with the background count (in this case, the presence of Ristul, which makes the Astral unworkably unclean).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-31T10:21:07-07:00","id":1559143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1553771-what-fictional-universe-s-would-you-live-in?p=1557403#post1557403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Finally, there's the <b>Kings of Hell </b>universe, which just seems like a ton of fun to live in!</div> </div> </div> </div>Kings of Hell would be fun, I agree.<br /> <br /> As would the <b>Bundheim</b> setting of D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> Though for less lewd possibilities, I might be willing to give <b>Shadow of the Demon Lord</b> a try.<br /> <br /> It's a lot more grimdark than typical D&amp;D, but at least Hell is only a temporary punishment, instead of a realm of eternal torment.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-06T18:36:46-07:00","id":1559259,"title":"","content":"One fictional setting I'd live in, is Blue Planet; it's the year 2199 and humanity has found a whole other, pristine blue-planet, to f*ck up; like they did to Earth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}